<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/geometry> skos:scopeNote "Use for explicit geometry semantics across vector graphics, geospatial features and glyph outlines. Spatial coordinates and measure ordinates must remain distinct."@en .
ageom:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
ageom:OrdinateShape rdfs:label "Ordinate Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using ageom:dimensionality, ageom:geometryType, ageom:hasM, ageom:hasZ. ageom:dimensionality takes at most one value; each is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype) greater than 0. Each value of ageom:geometryType is an IRI naming an instance of skos:Concept. ageom:hasM takes at most one value; each is an xsd:boolean literal. ageom:hasZ takes at most one value; each is an xsd:boolean literal."@en .
ageom:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using ageom:coordinatePrecision. ageom:coordinatePrecision takes an integer (rdfs:range xsd:integer)."@en .
